@startuml domain-er-diagram
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam entity {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor Black
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFF0
  BorderColor #CCCCAA
}
hide circle

title Portfolio Domain Model — Entity-Relationship view\n(the same model as domain-class-diagram.puml, expressed as tables)

entity "portfolio" as portfolio {
  * **portfolio_id** : CHAR(36) <<PK>>
  --
  * owner : VARCHAR(100)
  * balance : DECIMAL(19,2)
  * created_at : TIMESTAMP
}

entity "holding" as holding {
  * **holding_id** : CHAR(36) <<PK>>
  --
  * portfolio_id : CHAR(36) <<FK>>
  * ticker : VARCHAR(5)
  --
  UNIQUE (portfolio_id, ticker)
  CHECK (ticker matches ^[A-Z]{1,5}$)
}

entity "lot" as lot {
  * **lot_id** : CHAR(36) <<PK>>
  --
  * holding_id : CHAR(36) <<FK>>
  * initial_shares : INTEGER
  * remaining_shares : INTEGER
  * unit_price : DECIMAL(19,2)
  * purchased_at : TIMESTAMP
  --
  CHECK (initial_shares > 0)
  CHECK (remaining_shares >= 0)
  CHECK (remaining_shares <= initial_shares)
  CHECK (unit_price > 0)
  INDEX (holding_id, purchased_at)
}

portfolio ||--o{ holding : "owns"
holding   ||--|{ lot     : "was bought as"

note right of portfolio
  A portfolio owns **zero or more** holdings.
  Deleting a portfolio deletes its holdings
  and their lots (ON DELETE CASCADE) — the
  class diagram draws this as composition.
end note

note right of holding
  **UNIQUE (portfolio_id, ticker)** is what
  makes `Map<Ticker, Holding>` in the class
  diagram: at most one holding per ticker
  per portfolio.
end note

note right of lot
  **FIFO lives here — as an ordering, not a column.**
  Rows in a table have no inherent order. "Oldest
  lot first" means:
    ORDER BY purchased_at ASC
  Nothing in the schema enforces that a sale
  consumes lots in that order. Only the program
  does.
end note

note as ValueObjects
  **Where did Money, Price, ShareQuantity and Ticker go?**
  An ER model has no value objects — they dissolve into
  columns and constraints:
  |= Class diagram |= Here |
  | Money, Price | DECIMAL(19,2) |
  | ShareQuantity | INTEGER + CHECK (>= 0) |
  | Ticker | VARCHAR(5) |
  | PortfolioId, HoldingId, LotId | CHAR(36) primary keys |
  The OO version validates once, at construction, so an
  invalid value cannot exist. The table version re-checks
  on every INSERT and UPDATE.
end note

note as NotModelled
  **What is missing on purpose**

  **1. Behaviour.** sell(), buy(), reduce(),
  calculateCostBasis() have no equivalent — a table
  stores data, it does not compute. The FIFO rule and
  the money formulas live only in the program.

  **2. SellResult.** Not a table. proceeds, costBasis
  and profit are *computed and returned* by a sale;
  this kata never stores them. Persisting them would
  be a separate `transaction` table, which is out of
  scope for US-07.

  **3. Why the holding relation is one-or-many.**
  A sale that consumes the last lot also removes the
  holding, so a stored holding always has at least
  one lot. See sell-stocks-spec.md §6.2.
end note

ValueObjects .. lot
NotModelled .. portfolio

@enduml
